# AI Copilot Doctrine (Technical)
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **STATUS: BLUEPRINT / FUTURE STATE**
> Describes the technical architecture for the pending AI Copilot integration.

## Architecture
- Chat UX: Farfalle (assistant/executive-ai-assistant-main/farfalle-main)
- Tool Layer: Farfalle adapters → CRM whitelisted APIs
- Data Plane: Frappe CRM (DocTypes: CRM Lead, CRM Deal, CRM Organization, Contact, Communication, ToDo)
- Surfaces: Desk (forms + AI buttons), SPA (/crm), Server pages (/upload_leads, /crm/human_inbox), Chat (/crm/ai)

## Message Flow
1) User message → Farfalle intent + entities → tool plan
2) Tools executed against CRM endpoints (auth cookie/API key)
3) Responses aggregated → synthesized answer (+ links to CRM records)
4) Optional follow-up tool calls (e.g., create task, send email)

## Auth & CSRF
- Server-to-server: Service account on Frappe Cloud; maintain session cookie; include X-Frappe-CSRF-Token when required
- Delegated user: Farfalle operates on behalf of the logged-in user by forwarding session cookies via backend proxy
- Rate-limiting + retry for 429/5xx; exponential backoff

## Error Handling
- Tool error schema: { error_code, message, details?, suggestion? }
- Common errors: PERMISSION_DENIED, VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CSRF_TOKEN, RATE_LIMIT, NETWORK

## Data Privacy
- Scope tools by role; redact PII in logs; encrypt provider tokens; avoid storing CSV contents beyond job scope

## Limits
- Max rows per sync import: 5k (configurable)
- Tool timeouts: 30s default; long ops via job model and polling

## Observability
- CRM: structured logging via frappe.log_error, job logs; email draft realtime events (crm_email_draft_created)
- Farfalle: tool latency metrics, success/error rates, token usage

## Surfaces & Entry Points
- Desk AI Buttons: `crm/public/js/ai_actions.js` → `crm.api.agent.run`
- Human Inbox: `/crm/human_inbox` (review/send drafts)
- SPA Copilot: `/crm/ai` (embed Farfalle webchat or proxy)